  "result": "The O3 lesson is written, with a quiz and a cheat sheet to go with it. I couldn't run a word count, so I don't know if the lesson reaches 30 minutes. By my estimate it is roughly 3,900 to 4,300 words, which is inside the accepted range but may be a little under the full 4,500-word target. I didn't open the lesson in a browser either.\n\n- **Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory-in-an-agent.html`. It builds on the agent loop and teaches where each piece of the makerspace assistant's information should live. Sections:\n  1. The context window, using an NPC as the example.\n  2. What carries between steps, with a worked token count.\n  3. What carries between sessions, framed as a save file.\n  4. Retrieval, following one question through the pipeline.\n  5. A full trace of one booking request, plus a placement exercise.\n- **Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` has five items, and its key is `keys/0002.json`. Ask me for it when you want it. I haven't put any answers in this message.\n- **Cheat sheet:** `cheatsheets/0001-context-and-memory.html`. I also added `RESOURCES.md` and a line in `NOTES.md`.\n- **Sources:** Anthropic's context-engineering post is the primary source. I opened it and read it. The contextual-retrieval post I only saw through search snippets, so its numbers are from those.\n- **New misconception ids:** `NOTES.md` and the earlier key only gave me M1 to M6. For O3 I reused M3 and added M7 and M8, both new, in key 0002. M7 is \"a bigger window solves memory\". M8 is \"retrieval means the model read the whole manual\".\n- **No community added:** the lesson doesn't point you to an online community yet. Tell me if you want one.\n\n**Question for you:** do you want a shorter or longer version of the lesson? I can also start on the quiz now.",
